  "kind": "h9_14_seven_open_shadows_high_schedule_strict_g4_no_go",
  "proof": {
    "double_count": "For an 8-polytope boundary, g4=f3-6f2+21f1-56f0+126. Summing over vertex links and double-counting incidences gives sum_v g4(lk(v)) = 5 f4 - 24 f3 + 63 f2 - 112 f1 + 14*126. Hence every compact schedule must have summed value at least fourteen.",
    "independent_replay": "A no-project-import verifier derives h3 and h4 directly from the link h-vector definition, separately checks the expanded polynomial, and reproduces every schedule row.",
    "strict_local_bound": "For every vertex v, lk(v) is the boundary of a nonsimplex simplicial 8-polytope and inherits the Coxeter--Lanner missing-face order bound five. If g4(lk(v))=0, the generalized lower-bound equality theorem gives a nontrivial 3-stacked triangulation and hence a missing link face of order at least six. Therefore g4(lk(v))>=1 at all fourteen vertices."
  },
